#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-extract-structure.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A document ingested this way keeps its text in ocr/ and only a stub in sections/, which the documented sections/ grep cannot see. That asymmetry is why the corpus-grep checklist has a fourth tier. The run also records WHICH SOFTWARE made the pages, in ocr/run-context.json: a folio-run-context/v1 (cat-harness schemas/run-context.ts, the record test runs and QA reports use for the same question), naming the OCR engine, the rasteriser and each language model with its version and the sha256 of the bytes that ran. Two OCRs of one scan can read differently (\"Manual\" and \"Manval\"), and without it neither could be told from the other or reproduced."
msgstr ""

